[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1727","stub":{"id":"1727","section":"1. Clifty Bridge to Bee Creek","altname":"Caney Fork Gorge","river":"Caney Fork","difficulty":"IIItoV","states":["USA-TNN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The put-in is at Clifty Bridge accessed off Hwy. 70 near De Rossett/Pleasant Hill.","id":"109290","location":{"latitude":"35.891523","longitude":"-85.218"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":"14102","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The lead-in to Devil's Kitchen begins with a series of Class III-IV rapids that is recognized from the first real horizon line on the run as the river pinches in on river left. At the end of the lead-in a left-to-right move is made over a small ledge. The pool above the main drop is a good place to get your final line on the main drop in Devil's Kitchen. The big drop is a double drop that begins with a 6 foot slide right of center. Then the boater must move to the river left side to miss the \"bad\" hole on river right and execute a boof in the second drop finishing off by punching the bottom hole. Looking back up from the bottom, you know you have done some boatin.","id":"385","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Devil's Kitchen","distance":"1","difficulty":null,"approximate":false,"photoID":"41582"},{"type":"takeout","description":"A large pool signals the junction with Bee Creek. The take-out is on river right just below the Bee Creek junction.","id":"114529","location":{"latitude":"35.829258","longitude":"-85.2725"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"9.39","photoID":"14102","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"lqf3Q1jO6YTM7nT8NzouB","ext":"jpg","post_id":"LfN6XXsXCFkGZUuQBjLIQ","description":"","caption":"Scott's Gulf Wilderness State Park ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Allen Brown","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-21T16:18:43.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T16:18:43.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/lqf3Q1jO6YTM7nT8NzouB","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/lqf3Q1jO6YTM7nT8NzouB"}},{"id":"41582","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Mike McGee cooking in Devil's Kitchen. Devil's Kitchen throws everything but the kitchen sink at you. After a long lead in, a technical entrance, there's the nasty hole and undercuts waiting at the bottom. Good times, yes, good times.........","caption":"(RM) Devil's Kitchen - Mike","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"Mike McGee","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41582","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41582"}},{"id":"3163","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"Shot of one of the last rapids on the run from the Yellow Bluff Trail overlook ","caption":"Caney Fork Gorge \"Scotts Gulf\"","poi_name":"","subject":"Caney Fork Gorge","author":"Andrew McClanahan","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3163","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3163"}},{"id":"3168","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"This is the lead-in to Devils Kitchen.  Its really all one rapid cause there really are no real eddies and only seconds before your in the main drop.","caption":"Lead-in rapid to Devils Kitchen","poi_name":"Lead-in to Devils Kitchen","subject":"Caney Fork Whitewater","author":"Marty Montana","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3168","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3168"}},{"id":"3171","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"Typical of the big boulders strewn about this stream.  Choose your path wisely in places like this because the lines are sometimes tight and peppered with undercuts.","caption":"Boulder Choke","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Marty Montana","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3171","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3171"}},{"id":"10620","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"The Caney Fork gage isn't the easiest gage to find, or read for that matter. The gage can be seen from the upstream river left side of Clifty bridge. Look upstream for an old stone bridge support. The gage is bolted to the downstream side of the support. ","caption":"(RM) Caney Fork Gage","poi_name":"Caney Fork Gage","subject":"","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10620","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10620"}},{"id":"10621","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Scotts Gulf Road is as tough as any rapid you will find on the Caney Fork. 4wd with good clearance is recommended, however you can get down it with a 2wd as long as you have good clearance and know how to drive on seriously unmaintained roads. Nevertheless, 2wds WILL have problems in two or three very rutted/muddy spots that will become impassible from time to time. If you don’t have any problems, the drive down Scotts Gulf Road will take about 20 minutes one way. Good luck!!","caption":"(RM) Scotts Gulf Road","poi_name":"Scotts Gulf Road","subject":"","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10621","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10621"}},{"id":"41586","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"The land around the Caney Fork has more in common with swiss cheese then anything else. Immediately after a rain, it is not uncommon to find water flowing from the most unexpected places.","caption":"(RM) Water from rocks","poi_name":"","subject":"a rock","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41586","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41586"}},{"id":"41579","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"You can run the put-in rapid almost anywhere. If you screw it up, it might be a good idea to be the shuttle bunny instead of running the river.","caption":"(RM) Clifty Bridge Rapid","poi_name":"Clifty Bridge Rapid","subject":"","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41579","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41579"}},{"id":"39931","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"There is plenty of parking and empty beer bottles at the Upper Caney Fork put-in. From time-to-time cars are broken into, so be careful. The paddler's gage is on an old bridge pilon located on river left upstream of Clifty brige. The gage can be seen from Clifty bridge. And finally, look at all the boats, one of them doesn't make it to the take-out!","caption":"(RM) Upper Caney Fork Put-In","poi_name":"","subject":"Caney Fork Put-In","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/39931","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/39931"}},{"id":"6656","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"For the full-sized version of this picture, <a href=\"http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=3168\">click here</a>.","caption":"Lead-in rapid to Devils Kitchen (small photo)","poi_name":"Lead-in to Devils Kitchen","subject":"Caney Fork Whitewater","author":"Marty Montana","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6656","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6656"}},{"id":"883540","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"886230","description":"One of the last drops is 'thread the needle' and as of 5/14 has a tree just blow the main squeeze.  Easily ducked on the right, marked with orange tape you might see if you are looking for it from the top.  ","caption":"Tree below 'thread the needle'","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Clay Wright","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883540","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883540"}},{"id":"41580","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Devil's Kitchen throws everything but the kitchen sink at you. After a long lead in, a technical entrance, there's the nasty hole and undercuts waiting at the bottom. Good times, yes, good times.........","caption":"(RM) Devil's Kitchen","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"?","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41580","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41580"}},{"id":"41583","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Tim Madson going a has the right ingredients in Devil's Kitchen. (corny huh?) Devil's Kitchen throws everything but the kitchen sink at you. After a long lead in, a technical entrance, there's the nasty hole and undercuts waiting at the bottom. Check out the hole and undercuts on river right!! Good times, yes, good times.....","caption":"(RM) Devil's Kitchen from above - Tim","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"Tim Madson","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41583","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41583"}},{"id":"40454","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4060","description":"","caption":"Caney Fork Pin","poi_name":"none","subject":"Mark Hammock n Justin Owen","author":"Clay Wright","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40454","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40454"}},{"id":"14584","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6338","description":"At the put-in, we thought that we had plenty of water for the run. The old bridge gauge was reading 1.3’. In spite of many tributaries feeding in, it seemed like we were losing water as we paddled. It looks like a little more water is needed to fill the sieves near the end of the run & keep from scraping soooo many rocks.","caption":"Low Water Devils Kitchen","poi_name":"Devils Kitchen","subject":"Panorama of Devils Kitchen","author":"Jeff Macklin","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14584","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14584"}},{"id":"892306","ext":"jpg","post_id":"896206","description":null,"caption":"Surf waves at clifty at 1250 cfs","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Dave Fulcher","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/892306","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/892306"}},{"id":"14102","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3945","description":"See notes section of map for details.","caption":"Caney Fork Shuttle Route","poi_name":"","subject":"Caney Fork Shuttle route","author":"Geoff Kohl","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14102","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14102"}},{"id":"41585","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Mike McGee running one of many many fun drops on the Caney Fork","caption":"(RM) Mike somewhere on Caney Fork","poi_name":"Misc. Drop","subject":"Mike McGee","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41585","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41585"}},{"id":"3245","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5532","description":"a great view from the dry line","caption":"Devils Kitchen on the Caney Fork","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Butler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3245","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3245"}},{"id":"3250","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5532","description":"before the hike out & near hypothermia","caption":"Caney Fork boogie","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Butler aka Pops (team ELF)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3250","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3250"}},{"id":"3169","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"This is a stretch of class 3+ boogie below the kitchen before the numerous class 4 boulder garden rapids appear that the Caney Fork is infamous for.","caption":"Rapids below the Kitchen","poi_name":"Below the Kitchen","subject":"","author":"Marty Montana","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3169","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3169"}},{"id":"3170","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"This is a view from the Yellow Bluff trail.  Only a .3 mile walk from Scott's Gulf road and its the next trailhead past Virgin Falls trailhead on the left.  Well worth the walk.","caption":"Caney Fork Gorge Spectacular","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Marty Montana","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3170","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3170"}},{"id":"41576","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"There's plenty of parking and beer bottles at the put-in. Look closely, one of the boats doesn't make it to the take-out.","caption":"(RM) Caney Fork Put-In","poi_name":"Put-In","subject":"","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41576","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41576"}},{"id":"890376","ext":"png","post_id":"892730","description":"This wave comes in around 3.2' and gets great at 4'.  There's a smaller wave / hole upstream at lower levels, this was 5' guesstimated. ","caption":"Todd Town, Trailer Park Wave BIG water","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Clay Wright","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890376","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890376"}},{"id":"41584","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Dan Guthrie running on of many many drops on Caney Fork","caption":"(RM) Dan Somewhere on Caney Fork","poi_name":"Misc. Drop","subject":"Dan Guthrie","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41584","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41584"}},{"id":"42628","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6120","description":"","caption":"Canney Fork Ledge","poi_name":"?","subject":"Sean and Luke","author":"JC","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42628","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42628"}},{"id":"40455","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4060","description":"","caption":"Devil's Kitchen tony","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"Tony Robbins","author":"Clay Wright","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40455","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40455"}},{"id":"40456","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4060","description":"","caption":"Devil's Kitchen tony #2","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"Tony Robbins","author":"Clay Wright","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40456","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40456"}},{"id":"40453","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4060","description":"Stephen boofs in Devil's Kitchen from right slot","caption":"Stephen wRight slot","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"stephen wright","author":"clay wright","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40453","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40453"}},{"id":"3167","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5518","description":"Devils Kitchen Rapid, first big rapid on the river. Its within the first two miles of the run and marks the beginning of the first long stretch of rapids.  It has a committing lead in rapid.  Easy walk on the left.","caption":"Devils Kitchen","poi_name":"Devils Kitchen","subject":"Devils Kitchen","author":"Marty Montana","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3167","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3167"}},{"id":"41587","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Deveil's Kitchen has a fairly long entrace filled with chutes and zig-zagging from river right to left to right to...... well, you get the idea. You can shorten the portage of DK by hopping your way down to the last eddies before the main drop.","caption":"(RM) Devils Kitchen entrance","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen Entrance","subject":"Tim Madson","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41587","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41587"}},{"id":"41581","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5689","description":"Here's Marshall Fox making the final drops in Devil's Kitchen. Devil's Kitchen throws everything but the kitchen sink at you. After a long lead in, a technical entrance, there's the nasty hole and undercuts waiting at the bottom. Good times, yes, good times.........","caption":"(RM) Devil's Kitchen - Marshall","poi_name":"Devil's Kitchen","subject":"Marshall Fox","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41581","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41581"}},{"id":"42632","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6120","description":"","caption":"Scout","poi_name":"Devils Kitchen","subject":"Noboof Crew","author":"JC","poi_id":"385","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42632","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42632"}}],"detail":{"id":"1727","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The Caney Fork has a little of everything from play holes to ledge drops to fun boulder garden rapids. The put-in is at Clifty Bridge accessed off Hwy. 70 near De Rossett/Pleasant Hill (consult your Gazetteer). The first 3/4 mile is a flatwater warm-up. After a couple of easy rapids and past the trailer homes on river right, you come to Trailer Trash, a series of two very friendly wave holes that can be surfed until you are whopped or disoriented. Several Class IIIs follow that lead up to the top of Devil's Kitchen (Class V) where a distinct horizon line is a warning. See the description of Devil's Kitchen below. Scout and carry on river left. Immediately below Devil's Kitchen is a rock/boulder garden that we call Junk Yard (Lots of broken ledges, small bolders, and assorted collected debris). It loves to hang logs so pay attention. A consistent line that usually works is to start left side and keep working all the way left in the first part and then work from left to center to make the last drop in the center.\n\nThere are a number of Class III-IV ledges and boulder garden rapids that continue through a stretch that includes the beautiful Copper Cascades tributary that comes in from river right. Below Copper Cascades you will encounter a tighter more boulder garden section that has several nice Class III-IV rapids. After this you will reach the first lengthy pool. This is just over half way down the run. There is a trail that can be accessed at the end of this pool near a side stream. Follow the Polly's Branch Trail up and out of the gorge to access the Scott's Gulf Road or the Eastland Road. The river continues with numerous boulder gardens and ledge drops. After about 8 miles you will reach a tighter gorge with large polished boulders on the banks and in the stream. This section has several fun rapids with a bigger water feel. The last big rapid is Eye of the Needle. The main flow is in the center through a slot between boulders and then over a ledge drop angling back to the left. Following this rapid move all the way across to river left and run the rock garden below. A large pool signals the junction with Bee Creek. The take-out is on river right just below the Bee Creek junction.\n\nScott's Gulf Road to the Bee Creek confluence is now graded and graveled to within 200 yards of the bottom thanks to the Tennessee Wildlife Resources Agency. A great debt is owed to the Friends of Scott's Gulf who worked to ensure that the property has been protected. Additional information on the Caney Fork River take-out at Bee Creek, the Scott's Gulf Road access, and the Firestone-Bridgestone Centennial Wilderness can be found at [Scott's Gulf](%C3%83%C2%AF%C3%82%C2%BF%C3%82%C2%BDhttp:/www.centennialwilderness.com%C3%83%C2%AF%C3%82%C2%BF%C3%82%C2%BD).","average